control statements: 3 types

Types of Control Statements:

1. Decision-Making Statements(conditional)

if, if-else, else-if, nested if, switch

2. Looping Statements

for, while, do-while, enhanced for

3. Jump Statements

break, continue, return

  1. Decision-Making Statements
These statements execute code based on conditions.

  A. if statement :
Executes code when the condition is true.
  
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int age = 18;

        if (age >= 18) {
            System.out.println("Eligible");
        }
    }
}
  B. if-else statement :
Executes one block if true and another if false.
int num = 10;

if (num % 2 == 0) {
    System.out.println("Even");
} else {
    System.out.println("Odd");
}

  C. else-if ladder :
Checks multiple conditions.
int marks = 85;
if (marks >= 90) {
    System.out.println("A Grade");
} else if (marks >= 75) {
    System.out.println("B Grade");
} else if (marks >= 50) {
    System.out.println("C Grade");
} else {
    System.out.println("Fail");
}

D. Nested if
An if statement inside another if statement.
int age = 20;
int marks = 80;

if (age >= 18) {
    if (marks >= 50) {
        System.out.println("Eligible");
    }
}

E. switch statement
Used to select one option from multiple cases.
int day = 2;

switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
        break;

    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");
        break;

    default:
        System.out.println("Invalid day");
}
